# Architecture

## Version 1: Local MVP Architecture

DeliveryPulse will initially be built as a full-stack web application using Next.js.

## Components

### Frontend

The frontend will be built with Next.js, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS.

Responsibilities:

- Display project dashboard
- Display project details
- Provide forms for projects, risks, blockers, and milestones
- Display weekly status report

### Backend

The backend will use Next.js API routes.

Responsibilities:

- Handle CRUD operations
- Validate request data
- Apply business logic
- Calculate risk severity
- Calculate project health

### Database

The database will use PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM.

Responsibilities:

- Store projects
- Store risks
- Store blockers
- Store milestones
- Store status reports

## Initial Architecture Diagram

User Browser >>> Next.js Frontend >>> Next.js API Routes >>> Prisma ORM >>> PostgreSQL Database
